550/michigan-hire-texas-trev-alberts-athletic-director","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Dan Wetzel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on College Football Playoff bubble after the committee's third ranking?","description":"A conference-by-conference look at which teams are contending for the playoff, who's close and who's out.","published":"2026-11-18T03:42:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503628/cfp-playoff-2026-bubble-watch-week-third-ranking","type":"Story","byline":"Heather Dinich","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on the move? CFP committee's third top 25 and bracket of 2026","description":"A look at the new bracket based on the College Football Playoff committee's third set of rankings.","published":"2026-11-18T04:34:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50514170/cfp-2026-third-committee-top-25-bracket","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest surges into CFP top 12; top 4 unchanged while Texas jumps Notre Dame","description":"Alabama stayed at No. 3 despite some struggles on Saturday while two-loss Texas jumped one-loss Notre Dame for No. 5 in the CFP's latest rankings.","published":"2026-11-18T04:55:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50515993/wake-forest-surges-cfp-top-12-texas-jumps-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Pawn shop fighting 'Gold Digger' trademark filed by Jordon Hudson's company","description":"A California pawn shop is opposing a trademark application for \"Gold Digger\" filed by a company connected to Jordan Hudson, then-companion of Bill Belichick.","published":"2026-11-18T00:07:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/story/_/id/50514442/pawn-shop-fights-gold-digger-trademark-filed-hudson","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Anthony Olivieri","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma coach Venables shouts out Love's after Buc-ee's comment","description":"Venables showed love Sunday to Buc-ee's -- which is owned by an alumnus of the Sooners' next opponent, Texas A&M. So on Tuesday the coach repped the Oklahoma-based Love's.","published":"2026-11-17T22:23:36.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50513199/oklahoma-brent-venables-loves-travel-stop","type":"Story","byline":"J.J. Post","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football coaching carousel: Tracking every open job","description":"As the carousel spins, we'll keep you updated with all the comings and goings.","published":"2026-11-17T21:26:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50358611/2026-cfb-coaching-carousel-firings-hirings","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4881031/jamari-sharpe","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamari_Sharpe"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jamari Sharpe","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamari_Sharpe","description":"American football player (born 2003)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:24Z","intro":"Jamari Sharpe (born September 22, 2003) is an American college football defensive back for the Indiana Hoosiers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Sharpe was born September 22, 2003, in Miami, Florida. He attended Miami Northwestern Senior High School, where he played wide receiver on the school's football team before changing to cornerback in his senior year. Sharpe and Northwestern won a state championship in 2019. He also competed in track and field, placing sixth in the 100-meter dash and second on the 4 × 100 team at state finals."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"A three-star college football recruit, Sharpe committed to play for the Indiana Hoosiers beginning in 2022 as part of the school's highest-ranked recruiting class in program history. He redshirted the 2022 season after appearing in three games. In 2023, he played in all 12 games with nine starts, recording 22 tackles, three pass breakups, and one interception. He appeared in nine games with three starts in 2024, including a start in Indiana's 2024–25 College Football Playoff game against the Notre Dame Fighting Irish, recording 13 tackles, six pass breakups, one fumble recovery, and 0.5 sacks on the season.\nSharpe was named the likely starter for the 2025 season by head coach Curt Cignetti during preseason training camp. In a win against the Oregon Ducks, as Sharpe left the field with an injury, the broadcast showed Cignetti appearing to tell Sharpe to \"toughen up\"; Sharpe returned to the game one play later. Sharpe caught the game-sealing interception of a Carson Beck pass against the Miami Hurricanes in the 2026 College Football Playoff National Championship, which won Indiana their first national championship in program history."}]}}